.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
\-\-json opts into JSON. Help and version remain text. Duplicate global options fail before help/version short circuits.
.SH SAFETY
Removal refuses dirty worktrees and unproven ownership. Dry runs acquire no locks and perform no mutations; execution rechecks state. New workspaces record requested base source/ref and actual immutable starting commits. Fresh selection must fetch successfully; cached/local modes never fetch or silently fall back. Fresh previews report that fetching is required. Workspace removal preserves local branches. Repository removal unregisters while retaining the mirror, all refs and objects. Inspect repo list or repo show with --retained, then explicitly repo restore after ownership validation. Restore never fetches or adopts arbitrary directories. No storage purge is provided; network operations require explicit authorization. Modified or foreign generated AGENTS.md requires explicit consent. Crash records require manual inspection, never automatic recovery.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means success. 1 means an error on stderr, or a partial result on stdout. Inspect structured results before retrying.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
OUTPOST_HOME selects the state home, default ~/.outpost. OUTPOST_GIT_TIMEOUT_MS sets the Git timeout in milliseconds.
.SH OFFLINE GUIDANCE
Use outpost docs, outpost docs recovery, outpost skill show, or outpost skill path \-\-json.
